  "id": "hemispheric-dominance",
  "term": "hemispheric dominance",
  "definition": "Hemispheric dominance is the tendency for one cerebral hemisphere to play the leading role in a particular function, especially language or speech processing. In this context, it refers to assessing which side of the brain shows stronger involvement in processing speech-related sounds.",
